<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3">CRM Pipeline Stages & Funnel Configuration</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4">
            Model your unique sales process with custom pipeline stages that ensure sales discipline and provide 
            the clean data required for accurate revenue forecasting.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Custom Sales Funnel Modeling</h2>
        <p>
            No two sales processes are identical. Our pipeline configuration engine allows you to define 
            unlimited stages tailored to your specific go-to-market model. From initial 
            prospecting and technical qualification to legal review and final negotiation, 
            the system adapts to how you genuinely sell, ensuring high levels of platform 
            adoption by your sales team.
        </p>
        <p>
            Multiple distinct pipelines (e.g., "Direct Sales," "Channel Sales," "Renewals") can 
            be configured with their own unique stages and rules, supporting the diverse 
            revenue streams of complex organizations.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Stage-Gate Discipline and Criteria</h2>
        <p>
            Maintain the integrity of your sales data with configurable entry and exit criteria for 
            every stage. Require specific fields to be populated (e.g., "Decision Maker Identified") 
            or documents to be uploaded (e.g., "Signed NDA") before a deal can be moved forward 
            in the funnel. This "stage-gate" approach ensures that your pipeline metrics 
            underpin a rigorous and verifiable sales reality.
        </p>
        <p>
            Automated task generation on stage entry ensures that sales representatives are 
            immediately prompted for the "next best actions" required to move the deal 
            closer to resolution, maintaining commercial momentum.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Probability Weighting and Forecast Tuning</h2>
        <p>
            Associate a probability weighting (%) with every stage, representing the statistical 
            likelihood of a deal at that phase ultimately closing. These weightings 
            feed the weighted pipeline modeling engine, providing an automated and 
            objective view of anticipated revenue.
        </p>
        <p>
            As your sales team gains historical data, these stage weightings can be tuned 
            to reflect your actual historical win rates, continuously improving 
            the accuracy and predictability of your organizational sales forecasts.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

